cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Tissue Simulator: 3D simulated biological tissue section generator with network-based spatial analysis"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Eric
    family-names: Cramer
    email: ericscrum@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/emcramer/tissue_simulator"
url: "https://emcramer.github.io/tissue_simulator/"
abstract: >-
  Tissue Simulator is a Python package for generating 3D simulated biological
  tissue sections using random sphere packing algorithms. It supports 2D
  sectioning, network-based spatial analysis, graph-based cell type assignment
  via simulated annealing, tissue replicate generation matching target spatial
  statistics, and export to agent-based modeling frameworks such as PhysiCell.
keywords:
  - tissue simulation
  - sphere packing
  - spatial analysis
  - histology
  - agent-based modeling
  - physicell
  - bioinformatics
license: MIT
